# Part 1: stack template (Node/TypeScript web monorepo, plus the Python Home Assistant integration).
node_modules/
dist/
.vite/
*.tsbuildinfo
*.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Part 2: project rules, each with the reason it exists.

# Runtime data written by the dev stack and local runs. Only the demo library files the app serves
# stay tracked (one of them is 6.3 MB).
/data/*
!/data/demo-library/
/data/demo-library/*
!/data/demo-library/Rail Mount.gcode.3mf
!/data/demo-library/Card Holder (3 rows).gcode.3mf
!/data/demo-library/Number Plates.gcode.3mf
!/data/demo-library/Tire Rotation Markers.gcode.3mf
apps/api/data/
apps/api/prisma/data/
apps/bridge/data/
apps/bridge/apps/bridge/data/
# Bridge/demo runtime state written relative to CWD when a process is launched from `apps/`
# rather than its own workspace. Holds an installationId + runtimeToken, which are secrets.
# The known cause (a wrong hop count in the demo bootstrap's `repoRoot`) was fixed 2026-09-09 and
# the stray directory deleted, but this stays: the two entries above are the same class of bug from
# other paths, and the cost of being wrong here is committing a live credential.
apps/data/

# Ad-hoc 3MF fixtures dropped in the repo root while investigating a file (multi-megabyte,
# user-specific). Real fixtures live beside their tests or under /data/demo-library.
/*.3mf

# Transient BambuStudio CLI output written to CWD when the slicer (or a manual CLI probe)
# runs in-workspace. Slice output itself goes to SLICER_WORK_DIR (/tmp); this stray file
# lands wherever the CLI was launched from (the slicer workspace or the repo root).
apps/slicer/result.json
/result.json

# SEA download caches for the bridge and the native server. Their build output now goes to the
# shared /.artifacts/ (below); the two release/ folders are where older checkouts wrote it and
# can be deleted.
apps/bridge/.cache/
apps/server/.cache/
apps/bridge/release/
apps/server/release/

# Capacitor's platform trees are generated from the maintained mobile overlays.
# Firebase config is injected locally or through CI (release signing material is covered below).
apps/mobile/android/
apps/mobile/ios/
google-services.json

# Windows client build output and generated packaging images (signing material is covered below).
# Electron packages now go to /.artifacts/; the artifacts/ folder is where older checkouts wrote them.
apps/desktop/**/bin/
apps/desktop/**/obj/
apps/desktop/artifacts/
apps/desktop/PrintStream.Desktop/app.ico
apps/desktop/PrintStream.Desktop/Images/

# A developer's local scratch notes on work in progress, never shared.
docs/current-work-status.md

# Local SQLite files from tools and experiments; the app's database is PostgreSQL.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Deployment-local copies of the tracked *.example files, made at the repo root on a server.
/compose.yml
/nginx.conf

# Project-scoped MCP config: holds a per-install localhost token (Integrated
# Browser MCP), so it's developer-local, not shared/committed.
/.mcp.json

# Hand-made backups of the developer-local files above. Ignored by pattern so a
# `cp x x.bak` before a local experiment can't be swept into a commit by
# `git add -A`: the original is already ignored, but the copy was not.
*.bak

# ESLint results cache (`npm run lint`). Developer-local and machine-specific: it keys results
# on a content hash per file, so sharing it across machines or branches buys nothing and risks
# masking a real finding. CI always runs it cold.
.eslintcache

# Part 3: the shared block, last.
# Shared block (HYG-6), from winui-app-kit build/shared.gitignore. Paste it unchanged as the last part
# of every repo's .gitignore, so no earlier line can un-ignore what it covers. Change it in the kit.
/.artifacts/
/.windows-build/
/.worktrees/
.secrets/
.aws/
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example
tmp/
.backups/
*.pfx
*.cer
*.der
*.keystore
*.jks
local.properties
.vs/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
